			"__comment": "Static stand-in for the SHAFT_HALF peg GearboxRenderer/GearboxVisual normally draws poking out the two faces along the block's main axis. This file is itself baked UNROTATED (axis=y assumed); Create's own gearbox.json blockstate variants (x90/y90 for axis=x, x90/y180 for axis=z) rotate this whole model - shaft included - the same way they already rotate Bottom/Core/Top, so the stub ends up aligned with whichever axis the real peg would use without any extra rotation math here. Tune the 2px protrusion/position visually in-game (F3+T to reload resources) - this is a starting point, not a measured match to SHAFT_HALF's real dimensions.",
